
                   libyaz0 -- a fast yaz0 compression library

Purpose

    libyaz0 is a fast and efficient implementation of the Yaz0 compression
    algorithm used by Nintendo in their games since the Nintendo 64.

Origin

    The libyaz0 project was started in 2026 to address issues in existing Yaz0
    implementations and to provide a better (de)compressor for the Ocarina of
    Time Randomizer project.

    First and foremost, existing implementations of the algorithm usually
    operate on large buffers that require both the input and output files to
    be fully loaded into memory. This poses a problem for large files and
    constrained memory environments.

    Furthermore, many implementations leave room for improvement in terms of
    performance. libyaz0 aims to make use of modern CPU vectorization
    instructions such as SSE2, AVX2, and ARM Neon where possible.

    Lastly, most implementations are brittle and poorly tested. libyaz0 aims
    to include a comprehensive test suite to verify the correctness of the
    implementation.

