Compiling

    Download the latest source tarball, and then:

        tar -xvf libyaz0-x.y.z.tar.gz
        cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -S ./libyaz0-x.y -B /path/to/build-dir
        cmake --build /path/to/build-dir
        cmake --install /path/to/build-dir --prefix /path/to/install-dir

    You will need CMake 3.21 or later, as well as a C compiler that supports
    the C99 standard.

Versioning
    libyaz0 uses semantic versioning. Until the 1.0 release, no guarantee of
    API or ABI stability is made: any 0.x release may change the public
    interface.
